<p>Use one of the equivalent structural preflight routes below on <code>sequences.fasta</code>. Both require at least three records, unique first-token IDs, and non-empty sequences. They do not determine whether records are homologous, the right orthologs, or the right biological sequence type. The input is your unaligned FASTA file; no R package is required for the primary check.</p>
<h3 id="phylo-raw-fasta-r">R · base R (primary route)</h3>
<pre><code>read_fasta &lt;- function(path) {
  lines &lt;- readLines(path, warn = FALSE)
  records &lt;- list()
  for (line in trimws(lines)) {
    if (!nzchar(line)) next
    if (startsWith(line, ">")) {
      header &lt;- trimws(sub("^&gt;", "", line))
      tokens &lt;- strsplit(header, "\\s+")[[1]]
      id &lt;- if (length(tokens)) tokens[[1]] else ""
      if (!nzchar(id)) stop("STOP: empty FASTA identifier")
      records[[length(records) + 1L]] &lt;- list(id = id, seq = "")
    } else {
      if (!length(records)) stop("STOP: sequence text before first FASTA header")
      records[[length(records)]]$seq &lt;- paste0(records[[length(records)]]$seq,
                                                gsub("\\s+", "", line, perl = TRUE))
    }
  }
  ids &lt;- vapply(records, `[[`, character(1), "id")
  seqs &lt;- vapply(records, `[[`, character(1), "seq")
  if (length(records) &lt; 3L || anyDuplicated(ids) || any(!nzchar(seqs)) ||
      any(!nzchar(ids))) {
    stop("STOP: require &gt;=3 records, unique IDs, and non-empty sequences")
  }
  list(ids = ids, seqs = seqs)
}
